body: "## What shipped and what did not\nThe attribution-enforcement work delivered strict unknown-author rejection, SDK test-all author parity, and a public acknowledgeUnknownAuthorHistoryEvents primitive with hardened error handling. Its acceptance criteria also stated that the five stranded events would be dispositioned and health would return ok:true. The primitive exists; the disposition was never executed against this repository, and there is no CLI or MCP path to execute it.\n\n## Why the disposition is a judgement call\nAcknowledgment records a reviewer, an attributed author, and a reason against immutable events. That is a maintainer decision about who is accountable for five specific historical mutations, not a mechanical cleanup, which is why it must be run deliberately rather than folded into a sweep.\n\n## Boundary\nNo history rewriting. No baseline movement. No hand-attribution of legacy pre-baseline events — only the five post-baseline actionable ones. Preventing future unknown-author events is the harness identity work, not this item."
